the Duchesse de Guermantes. Geneviève Halévy Bizet Straus; Laure de Sade, Comtesse de Adhéaume de Chevigné; and Élisabeth de Riquet de Caraman-Chimay, the Comtesse Greffuhle--these were the three superstars of fin-de-siècle Parisian high society who, as Caroline Weber says, \"transformed themselves, and were transformed by those around them, into living legends: paragons of elegance, nobility, and style.\" All well but unhappily married, these women sought freedom and fulfillment by reinventing themselves, between the 1870s and 1890s, as icons. At their fabled salons, they inspired the creativity of several generations of writers, visual artists, composers, designers, and journalists. Against a rich historical backdrop, Weber takes the reader into these women's daily lives of masked balls, hunts, dinners, court visits, nights at the opera or theater. But we see as well the loneliness, rigid social rules, and loveless, arranged marriages that constricted these women's lives.","pageCount":715,"publicationYear":2018,"displaySummary":"At their fabled salons, they inspired the creativity of several generations of writers, visual artists, composers, designers, and journalists. Against a rich historical backdrop, Weber takes the reader into these women's daily lives of masked balls, hunts, dinners, court visits, nights at the opera or theater. But we see as well the loneliness, rigid social rules, and loveless, arranged marriages that constricted these women's lives.","primaryTopic":"Intellectual Biography","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Biography","confidence":"high","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Biography","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Biography","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book focuses on the lives of three key women and their influence on Parisian society and culture during a specific historical period, positioning it primarily within Biography while